This is the ggplot2 mailing list; general R help questions are off-topic here.

>
> I'm trying to geocode a list of descriptive locations and return coordinates
> to plot on GIS. I have a dataframe of Twitter users and isolated the
> locations column (column 12) giving a list of locations. Then ran a loop:
>
> for (i in data.frame[[12]]){geocode(i)

You need to assign the result of geocode to something, e.g.,

geocodes <- vector(length=ncol(data.frame))
names(geocodes) <- data.frame[[12]]

for (i in data.frame[[12]]){

    geocodes[i] <- geocode(i)
}

Best,
Ista

